#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:11
msgid ""
"Everything added on this site — characters, value types, value options, "
"sources, translations, and the reasons given for changes — is public and "
"dedicated to the public domain under <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/"
"publicdomain/zero/1.0/\">CC0 1.0</a>: anyone may use it in any way, without "
"asking. You agree to this when you sign up, or the first time you add "
"something."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:12
msgid ""
"Only add what you have the right to share. Facts and your own words are "
"fine; do not paste text copied from books or websites unless its license "
"allows it."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:13
msgid ""
"Your username is shown with everything you add and in the public edit "
"history. If you delete your account, your contributions stay on the site, "
"credited to “former-contributor” and a number."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:16
msgid "What is stored about you"
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:18
msgid "Your username, which is public."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:19
msgid ""
"Your email address, which is not shown publicly and never sold. It is used "
"to sign in (with your username or email), to confirm your account, to reset "
"your password and to tell you about changes to your account's security. It "
"is passed to Resend only so that these emails can be delivered. There are no "
"newsletters."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:20
msgid ""
"Your password, stored only in a form that cannot be turned back into the "
"password."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:21
msgid ""
"If you turn on two-factor sign-in: its secret key and your recovery codes."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:22
msgid ""
"When you joined, when you last signed in, and when you agreed to the "
"contribution terms (and which version)."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:23
msgid ""
"For each signed-in device: the browser, IP address and last activity, so you "
"can see and sign out other devices on your account page. Security emails "
"about your account also show the time, IP address and browser of the change."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:24
msgid ""
"If you send a “Needs review” report: your note, the page, the time and, if "
"you are signed in, your username. It is not stored with your IP address."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:25
msgid ""
"To limit heavy use of the report form and the API, your IP address is used "
"only in scrambled form, as a counter that is deleted after an hour or less."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:26
msgid ""
"Cookies: for signing in and security, for one-time notices on the next page, "
"and to remember your choice of language and of common or scientific names. "
"No advertising, analytics or tracking cookies; no scripts or fonts from "
"other companies."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:29
msgid "Where it is kept"
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:31
msgid ""
"The site runs on a server rented from Hostinger, in the United States. Email "
"is sent through Resend, in the United States."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:32
msgid ""
"The server's web logs (IP address, page requested, browser) are kept for 14 "
"days. The site's own logs (time, page requested, browser) are limited in "
"size and overwritten as new entries arrive."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:33
msgid ""
"The database is backed up every night; the server keeps 30 days of backups, "
"and the administrator keeps a copy off the server."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:34
msgid ""
"When something goes wrong, the site emails an error report to its "
"administrator through Resend. It can include your username, IP address, "
"browser, the page and what you had just submitted (passwords, codes and keys "
"are hidden)."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:37
msgid "Your choices"
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:39
#, python-format
msgid ""
"See and change your email addresses and password, turn on two-factor sign-"
"in, and sign out other devices on <a href=\"%(account_url)s\">your account "
"page</a>."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:40
msgid ""
"Delete your account from your account page (“Delete my account”; your "
"password is asked again). Your email addresses, password, two-factor "
"settings and signed-in sessions are deleted at once, and your username is "
"replaced. The dates you joined, last signed in and agreed to the terms stay "
"with your contributions. Copies made before then (backups, and emails "
"already sent) are not changed; the server's backups expire after 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: characters/templates/characters/privacy.html:41
msgid ""
"Questions about your data: <a "
"href=\"mailto:contact@fungalcharacters.org\">contact@fungalcharacters.org</"
"a>."
msgstr ""

